Generalized regular expressions over a finite alphabet allow union, concatenation, Kleene star and complement relative to all finite words. Star height is the maximum number of nested stars; Boolean operations do not themselves increase it. For a regular language $L$, minimize this height over all generalized expressions defining $L$. Ask whether one finite bound works for every regular language. \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]} \href{https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/handle/10023/12024}{[S2]}

